  "note": "Document-first business frontend with direct CV editing, template-Mod import/selection and structured job analysis using native text-generation runners. CV imports use native owner-session CLI threads in the wrapper; existing model and permission defaults remain native. The app backend is rebuilt and pinned separately; installed T3 remains untouched. The shared CV content editor, separate form captions and per-entry PDF-inclusion controls are built, browser-verified and deployed. The frontend build was completed without source maps; native provider and permission behavior remains unchanged. The wrapper's empty Lua-list correction is deployed. The v2 form-Primitives renderer reuses the content editor with configurable labels in the normal CV workspace on the prototype branch. Its separate frontend/server/build commands were removed; the regular candidate app build and browser flow pass. This branch-only integration has not been deployed to the production application. Concurrent branding assets are retained. Thread details no longer render workspace/environment selection or version-control controls, including saved visibility overrides and menu/settings choices. The active app uses only its same-origin web server; stored foreign targets are retained but not connected. Browser/recording and peer RPC/MCP handlers, remote followers, desktop activation, native mobile client access and automatic settlement are retired. Legacy data/contracts remain readable. Application and chat views share the overview breadcrumb; Diagnostics UI, workspace defaults and snooze triggers are retired. The legacy chat archive view and extra optional-chat hint are removed. Legacy business chat events and the old Pi session were subsequently purged from active storage on explicit user request, with a consistent backup; current native chats remain unchanged. Full retirement of other previously marked native features remains incomplete.",
